<h2 id="browser-recovery">Optionally keep one copy on this browser</h2>
<p>Browser recovery is <strong>off by default</strong> in the public workspace and all converters. Open Keep work on this browser, optional. Read the privacy notice, acknowledge that the copy contains private notes in unencrypted browser storage, and choose Enable browser recovery. Anyone using this browser profile may restore it. Do not enable it on a shared device unless that is acceptable.</p>
<p>Once enabled, changed workspace writing is saved after a short pause; Save recovery now requests an immediate save. The status distinguishes pending changes from a saved copy. Only one Draft to Page tab can write the origin-wide copy. Another tab must pause saving or close before you can restore or remove it. Browsers without the required locking support offer private file backups instead.</p>
<p>The copy contains article fields, source notes, audience, purpose, article type, and saved review questions. It excludes pending imports, original Word files, recovered images, unsaved passage/link/image/table preparation, private collections, checkpoint history, approval, credentials, and publishing settings. Apply prepared writing or save a review note first to include it. No upload, AI request, account history, or device sync is added.</p>
<ol><li>On return, a saved copy is offered without replacing writing or resuming saving.</li><li>Choose Review saved browser copy. Compare every source and article field, including fields that will become empty. Review notes preserve explicit JSON list boundaries.</li><li>Acknowledge the comparison and local storage consent, then choose Restore reviewed copy and resume saving. Valid current writing is checkpointed before replacement; a failed checkpoint keeps it intact. Restore clears export approval and resets publishing choices.</li><li>Editing current writing or receiving a storage change clears the comparison acknowledgement. Review the copy again. Finish or clear pending imports before restoring.</li></ol>
<p>Pause saving, keep copy flushes eligible pending writing, then stops saving in this tab. Remove browser copy asks for confirmation, deletes stored data and stops saving while keeping open writing. Clear this writing desk includes the saved browser copy in its confirmation; if safe deletion fails or another tab owns it, current writing is kept. Browser site-data settings can remove a copy when storage access is blocked.</p>
<p>Storage errors stop saving and explain that newer writing may remain only in the open tab. Browser data can be evicted, cleared, or unavailable in private mode. There is no recovery guarantee. Keep a downloaded private backup for important work and check the file on your device. This optional feature is separate from the private pilot, which has no browser recovery.</p>
